### Why steps 1 and 4 were refused
This is the **already root-caused T-43 regression**, not a mistake in the sequence. In `assertMutationSandboxed` (`packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts`, live in `dist/index.js`), the predicate is `resolve(HOME) !== resolve(homedir())`, but on POSIX `homedir()` reads `$HOME` at process start — so `resolve(HOME) === resolve(homedir())` in every boot that sets `HOME` at spawn. The guard therefore cannot distinguish a sandbox home from the real home and refuses the very recipe its own message prescribes. Confirmations found in-repo: the QA record `evidence/platform/workmate-guard-spawn/20260917T032539Z/result.json` (with a `proposed.patch`, **not applied**), and `AGENTS.md` §T-43 requiring QA boots to use `HOME=<sandbox>` — which is exactly this boot (`HOME=/tmp/mpd-wm-home-NAC0K3`, `DSH_HOME=/tmp/mpd-wm-dsh-7lbrOS`).

I did **not** work around it: the override must be in the plugin host's environment at spawn (`process.env` only — the workmate plugin has no config-file surface, and dsh has no hot reload, T-21), so neither remediation is reachable from inside this session. I also did not hand-write library files to fake a successful init.

To make the sequence pass, the host must be booted with `MPD_DSH_WORKMATE_ALLOW_REAL_HOME=1` (deliberate override), or the regression must be fixed per the proposed patch + rebuild + spawn-shape tests.

